  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 125 PM CST Wed Nov 25 2026\n\nFriday through Wednesday:\n\nDry weather is expected during the day Friday between the\ndeparting strong low well to the east and an approaching\nshortwave from the west. Temps will be a bit milder Fri, with\nhighs in the mid to upper 40s. Models are then in decent\nagreement with a shortwave swinging through Friday night into\nSaturday morning. Given the strength of this wave along with a\nbrief shot of deeper moisture, thinking there will be a brief\nround of light rain chances. Models aren't spitting out much QPF\nyet though and the NBM is thus still coming in dry, so kept the\nforecast dry for the moment. Wouldn't be surprised at the need\nfor precip chances in the forecast soon though. Winds Saturday\nwill be out of the southwest behind the shortwave, allowing for\neven milder conditions, with highs approaching or hitting 50. \n\nAnother shortwave is progged to move through on Sunday, with a\nsurface low passing by well to the southeast. 12Z guidance is\nshowing the low track would keep precip mainly out of the\nforecast area, though the southeast could get clipped by some\nlight rain. Dry weather is then expected Monday through at \nleast Tuesday as high pressure moves through the region. Cooler\ntemps early next week are likely to warm back above normal for\nmid-week. \n\nDDV",
